# Rust build output
/target
**/target

# Local VibeWise learning notes (not versioned)
.vibe-wise/

# Logs
*.log

# Keys and secrets (never version these)
*.key
*.env
.env*
*.pem
*secret*

# Any config.json in the tree, the root one and any nested one (the daemon's
# real one lives in %APPDATA%, so nothing here may be committed)
config.json

# Scratch notes and research from the earlier session: they stay on disk, they
# are not published (the research tree quotes other projects' own docs)
/PLAN.md
/RESEARCH.md
/question.md
/handover_2.md
/docs/plans/
/docs/research/

# The private scope note for the orchestrator and the user: our eyes only
/docs/scope.md

# The session orientation file: it lives at the root, it is a session artefact,
# not project content. The versioned memory is docs/modularity\.
/compact.md

# The working notes of the current session: the handover, the test checklists,
# the decision log and the two specs. They stay on disk, they are not published.
/HANDOVER.md
/testing.md
/testing_final.md
/DECISIONS-2026-10-17.md
/SPEC3-SCRIPTING.md
/PACK-SPEC-PROPOSAL.md
/finish.md

# Documentation and keys are the same kind of thing: ours, never versioned. A README is
# the one exception, because a repository with no README is a repository nobody can start.
# Everything else (design, decisions, progress, the pack spec, the handover, the changelog)
# lives on disk and leaves this machine only if it is pasted somewhere by hand.
*.md
*.markdown
*.txt
*.pdf
*.docx
*.odt
*.rtf
!README.md
!**/README.md

# release-notes/ is ignored like every other doc *except* for the file the release
# workflow reads out of the checkout: `release-notes/<tag>.md` is the release body, and the
# build fails outright when it is missing (release.yml, "the release notes are missing").
!release-notes/*.md
